research/audit/wave8-judge-adjudications.jsonl:5:{"id":"lem-paracompact-hausdorff-cover-shrinking","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"602d1e306532760f54b6c07170bc2f711bc331e54d94a9b7ede3fe9e4cdffadf","outcome":"confirmed_nonfatal","item_sha256":"51ecae7021ef8d83ac64c6fbdb32a145a4124a6b7642e31de5c76a01d07bf0a8","verdict_item_sha256":"55760f96650fadd4302ed753ecf4626d7830798a3509e26d1b46929082c1464b","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-09T08:03:46Z","note":"F1 is locally compressed, because the library's bare definition of refinement does not imply covering. Its cited source def-paracompact-space nevertheless states the exact fact step 1.1 uses: 'every open cover U of X has an open refinement V which covers X and is locally finite,' and repeats this as 'there is a locally finite open cover V'. A competent reader restores the omitted word from the cited definition in seconds. This is nonfatal citation compression, so R1 licenses no edit."}
