research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-thm-componentwise-limits-and-continuity-r2.prompt.md-415-
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-thm-componentwise-limits-and-continuity-r2.prompt.md-416-Let $m \in \mathbb{N}$ with $m \ge 1$, with vector-valued functions, their
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-thm-componentwise-limits-and-continuity-r2.prompt.md-417-components $f_i = \pi_i \circ f$, their limits and their continuity as in
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-thm-componentwise-limits-and-continuity-r2.prompt.md-418-[[def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity]].
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-thm-componentwise-limits-and-continuity-r2.prompt.md-419-
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-thm-componentwise-limits-and-continuity-r2.prompt.md-420-1. **Continuity is componentwise.** Let $(X,d_X)$ be a metric space, $A \subseteq X$,
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-thm-componentwise-limits-and-continuity-r2.prompt.md-421-   $f : A \to \mathbb{R}^{m}$ and $a \in A$. Then $f$ is continuous at $a$ if and
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-thm-componentwise-limits-and-continuity-r2.prompt.md-422-   only if every component $f_i : A \to \mathbb{R}$ $(i<m)$ is continuous at $a$.
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-thm-componentwise-limits-and-continuity-r2.prompt.md-423-2. **Limits are componentwise.** Let $A \subseteq \mathbb{R}$, let $c$ be a limit
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-thm-componentwise-limits-and-continuity-r2.prompt.md-424-   point of $A$ ([[def-limit-point-r]]), let $f : A \to \mathbb{R}^{m}$ and let
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-thm-componentwise-limits-and-continuity-r2.prompt.md-425-   $L \in \mathbb{R}^{m}$. Then $\lim_{x\to c} f(x) = L$ if and only if
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-thm-componentwise-limits-and-continuity-r2.prompt.md-426-   $\lim_{x\to c} f_i(x) = L_i$ for every $i<m$ ([[def-function-limit]]).
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-thm-componentwise-limits-and-continuity-r2.prompt.md-427-3. **Algebra.** Let $(X,d_X)$, $A$, $a$ be as in clause 1, let
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-thm-componentwise-limits-and-continuity-r2.prompt.md-428-   $f, g : A \to \mathbb{R}^{m}$ be continuous at $a$ and let $\lambda \in \mathbb{R}$.
--
